  "worked_solution": "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{\u2032}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{\u2032}(t)}=sL{f(t)}-f(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{\u2032}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{\u2032}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-2s}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2s}{s(s-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>2.$",
